Adapt OpenTUI build.zig for Zig 0.16.0 (partial).

lang/zig on OpenBSD provides 0.16.0; upstream opentui v0.3.4
targets 0.15.2.  The Zig 0.15->0.16 stdlib removed several APIs
used by this build script.  This patch adds 0.16.0 to the
supported versions list and marks the remaining incompatibilities
with FIXME comments for manual resolution:

 - std.fs.cwd() removed (0.16 requires explicit Dir handles)
 - std.mem.trimRight removed (replace with index-based slicing)
 - b.graph.host removed (use b.host or another API)
 - b.graph.env_map removed (use std.process.getEnvVarOwned
   or the new env var API)

The uucode vendored dependency needs a manual fix:
  b.modules.put(b.dupe(...), ...)  ->  b.modules.put(b.allocator, b.dupe(...), ...)

Override via: zig build --system uucode=/path/to/patched/uucode

Remove this patch when upstream opentui supports Zig 0.16.

